From: =?UTF-8?q?Micha=C5=82=20Szczepaniak?= <m.szczepaniak.000@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:16:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gobi: read the slot IMEI regardless of the ESN

gobi_get_ids_cb() only looked at the IMEI when the modem reported no
ESN (or "0"). Modems that report both, like the MSM8974 modem on the
Moto X 2014 (ESN 8093D413), never stored the IMEI, so the slot was
never added, ofono_slot_driver_started() was never called and the
slot manager never became ready.

The slot needs the IMEI in every case, so read it directly. Also stop
treating user_data as a cb_data: it is the modem, so the old failure
path dereferenced the wrong type.
---
 plugins/gobi.c | 29 +++++++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plugins/gobi.c b/plugins/gobi.c
index e034b9b..bea8c03 100644
--- a/plugins/gobi.c
+++ b/plugins/gobi.c
@@ -227,22 +227,23 @@ static int qmi_wwan_set_pass_through(const char *interface, char value)
 static void gobi_get_ids_cb(struct qmi_result *result, void *user_data)
 {
 	char *str;
-	struct cb_data *cbd = user_data;
-	ofono_devinfo_query_cb_t cb = cbd->cb;
 
-	str = qmi_result_get_string(result, QMI_DMS_RESULT_ESN);
-	if (!str || strcmp(str, "0") == 0) {
-		str = qmi_result_get_string(result, QMI_DMS_RESULT_IMEI);
-		if (!str) {
-			CALLBACK_WITH_FAILURE(cb, NULL, cbd->data);
-			return;
-		} else {
-			ofono_info("Got IMEI %s", str);
-			l_strlcpy(imei, str, sizeof(imei));
-			gobi_slot_driver_startup_check();
-		}
+	if (qmi_result_set_error(result, NULL)) {
+		ofono_warn("Unable to get the modem IDs");
+		return;
 	}
-   l_free(str);
+
+	str = qmi_result_get_string(result, QMI_DMS_RESULT_IMEI);
+	if (!str) {
+		ofono_warn("Modem reported no IMEI");
+		return;
+	}
+
+	ofono_info("Got IMEI %s", str);
+	l_strlcpy(imei, str, sizeof(imei));
+	l_free(str);
+
+	gobi_slot_driver_startup_check();
 }
 
